            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ToastySpice5956"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Perfect. Honey mustard or hot mustard is always my top choice for dipping nuggets or fried tenders in and this one is perfect! I used Trader Joe’s hot honey which is much hotter than Mike’s hot honey. I could go with even more spice but the family said it was hot enough. Hot, sweet, tangy, perfect!",
            "datePublished": "2025-03-19T00:56:07.787Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KBPlace"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Like other people, I reversed the quantities of the mustards, using two tablespoons of the dijon, and one of yellow. I also added about 3/4 teaspoon of smoked paprika. It was delicious, and even my picky mother thought it was delicious, and perfect for the chicken koftas I made.",
            "datePublished": "2026-04-04T18:18:04.642Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TrendyRibs3280"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Perfect! Just the flavor I was going for! Tried with about a tsp or so of smoked paprika mixed in as well…. Smacks!",
            "datePublished": "2025-04-09T23:47:07.975Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "IcyMash4316"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Make this 1-2 times a week and use on garden salads, gyro salads, and as a dipping sauce for wings etc. so easy and easy to adjust. I always now use 1/2 mayo and 1/2 plain greek yogurt and make a double recipe. I like to have it in the fridge as I find my family can almost always combine it with leftovers and feed themselves snacks",
            "datePublished": "2023-01-08T20:30:06.831Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Karen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Five stars, but with a major modification: Done entirely in error, but the results were incredible. My husband was helping me in the kitchen and I tasked him with making this sauce for our Chicken Strips dinner. In error, he used 2 tablespoons of our good quality DRY mustard (mustard powder) instead of using prepared yellow mustard like the recipe states. No other changes were made. It was hands-down the best mustard dipping sauce I have ever tasted.",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-23T15:44:03.957Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Yadayada Yanyan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a very tasty recipe. Personally, I like it a little spicier, so I tried adding about 1/2 tsp of Japanese Mustard (karashi). It's from the same mustard family, so the flavor blends well with the rest of the dish, resulting in a crisp taste.",
            "datePublished": "2024-10-16T20:45:11.319Z"
          },
